# Microsoft SSO (Entra ID / Azure AD) Integration

## Background

AgentRadar currently uses email + password authentication backed by a JWT access/refresh token pair. The `users` table stores a `password_hash` (NOT NULL), a `role`, and a `tenant_id`. The goal is to let enterprise users sign in via their Microsoft 365 / company Azure AD account and automatically land in the correct role — with zero changes required to the JWT/refresh flow that the rest of the app already uses.

---

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Which SSO flow to use?**
> - **Option A — OAuth 2.0 Authorization Code flow (recommended)**: Redirect to Microsoft login → Microsoft redirects back to AgentRadar with an auth code → backend exchanges code for ID token → issue our own JWT. Most secure, works for any deployment.
> - **Option B — MSAL.js on the frontend only**: Microsoft SDK runs in the browser, gets an ID token, sends it to our backend which just verifies and issues JWT. Simpler frontend setup, slightly less backend control.
>
> The plan below assumes **Option A** (backend-initiated OIDC). Let me know if you prefer the frontend-only MSAL approach.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **How should role assignment work for new SSO users?**
> - **Option 1 — Default role on first login**: All first-time Microsoft SSO users get `analyst` role by default. A super-admin can promote them later.
> - **Option 2 — Azure AD Group mapping**: Map Azure AD security groups to AgentRadar roles (e.g., `AgentRadar-Admins` group → `admin`, `AgentRadar-Analysts` group → `analyst`). Requires extra Azure AD API call during login.
> - **Option 3 — Email domain whitelisting only**: Users from your company domain auto-get a role you configure at the tenant level.
>
> I recommend **Option 1** as the safest starting point, with a path to Option 2.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Which Azure AD tenant(s) to allow?**
> - **Single-tenant**: Only users from your one organization can sign in (most common for internal tooling).
> - **Multi-tenant**: Any Microsoft organization's users can sign in (useful if you sell to multiple companies).
>
> I'll plan for **single-tenant** but the config will be easy to switch.

